<!-- Display configuration of the built-in panel. The framework finds it by
     port (130), because the display HAL reports its own display ID.

     The brightness table is measured on the panel (white, 20 % window). The
     display HAL writes panel level int(1 + backlight * 4093); the kernel maps
     levels above 2048 onto the panel's high-brightness band, where only white
     gets brighter (mid greys stay put, colours oversaturate).

     - Brightness is linear in nits, so the slider and the brightness ramps
       (both HLG over brightness) are perceptually even. Only evenDimmer can
       give brightness -> backlight a shape; it is used for that alone.
     - Floor: level 10, 2.0 nits. Top: level 3480, 1151 nits.
     - The manual range ends at level 2048 (757 nits), the high-brightness
       transition. The band above is for sunlight. -->
<displayConfiguration>
  <!-- backlight -> nits for the whole panel. The framework cuts it to the
       range of the overlay (brightness.xml). evenDimmer below has the same
       points inside that range and is the map in use. -->
